{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "87068f4e-7bb9-8ea1-ac6b-38fb418f8283",
  "created_at": "2026-03-12T09:36:30-04:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Utilities",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Ivan Pina",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tony Ferreira",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T09:33:05-04:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Utilities billing, this is Tony. Good morning."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T09:33:08-04:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hey, good morning Tony. Ivan Pina here. So I'm just standing in the spare room with my coffee, it's the only spot in the house where I can get a signal, and I've got exactly one bar. So if I cut out, that's why."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T09:33:25-04:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem, I'll talk slow. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T09:33:30-04:00",
      "duration": 25,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, so I got my water and sewer bill yesterday and it's for a whole quarter. Three months. I'm used to a monthly thing from my old place, so honestly this one's got me irritated. Why is it a quarter, and how are you counting the dates? The period on it says something like December to the end of February, but the bill came in March."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T09:33:55-04:00",
      "duration": 20,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure. Newport bills water and sewer quarterly, so each bill covers about three months of use. The meter gets read at the end of that stretch, then the bill is calculated and mailed out, so there's a lag. That's why the service dates end a little before the date on the bill."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T09:34:15-04:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So the dates on there are the read dates, not when you printed it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T09:34:21-04:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Because I looked at it and thought, that's a lot of days for a winter bill. I'm barely home, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T09:34:30-04:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right, the service dates are from the previous reading to the latest one. The bill date is separate, it's when it was issued. If you want, I can look at the reading dates with you."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T09:34:43-04:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Nah, that's fine, I get it now. It's just a pain when the number lands all at once. Can you send me a duplicate copy though? Mine's got a coffee ring on it already and I want a clean one. By email, if you can."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T09:35:00-04:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yep, I can do that. What email do you want it sent to?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T09:35:06-04:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hang on, it's gonna cut out. [line breaks up] Can you hear me?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T09:35:12-04:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I lost you for a second there. Say that again?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T09:35:17-04:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I said, can you just send it to the email you've got on file? I haven't changed it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T09:35:24-04:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can do that. I'll send it to the one on the account, and it should be in your inbox shortly. Check spam in case it lands there."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T09:35:35-04:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Perfect. And one more thing. Can I pay it at a bank? Like, does any bank take the payment, or does it have to be somewhere specific? Where do you actually accept payments?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T09:35:48-04:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Banks aren't set up to take it, so a bank teller won't be able to process it. You can pay in person at City Hall, or you can mail a check with the stub from the bill. The stub has the mailing address printed right on it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T09:36:06-04:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, so City Hall or mail it in. Got it. I'll mail it, I've got stamps somewhere."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T09:36:13-04:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That works. Just keep the stub attached to the check so it gets matched to your account."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T09:36:20-04:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Will do. Alright Tony, thanks. I'm gonna go refill this coffee and find some better reception."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T09:36:27-04:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sounds good, Ivan. Have a good one."
    }
  ],
